is_anomaly: true
faulty_devices: srv1
diagnosis_text:
Affected component: Campus DNS service on srv1 (BIND/named). The daemon is running, but it is configured as an authoritative-only server with recursion disabled.

Mechanism: PC1 (and likely other clients) use srv1 as their resolver (pc1 /etc/resolv.conf → nameserver 10.5.0.4). When a user browses the Internet, queries for external names are sent to srv1. Because BIND is set to “recursion no”, it refuses those queries, so lookups for sites like www.google.com are answered with REFUSED. Applications then stall while retrying/falling back (for example to DoH), so pages “hang” and then “catch up,” which feels like a slow/overloaded Internet link even though the transport path is fine.

Localization and evidence:
- srv1 /et
